    <node id="薛烛">
      <data key="d0">薛烛</data>
      <data key="d1">人物</data>
      <data key="d2">Xue Zhu (薛烛) was a skilled swordsmith and craftsman from the ancient state of Yue (越国). He was one of the disciples of Ou Yezi (欧冶子), a legendary figure in Chinese metallurgy and sword-making. As a resident of Yue, Xue Zhu was renowned for his expertise in forging swords and was entrusted with significant responsibilities in this domain. He was tasked by Fan Li (范蠡), a prominent Yue official and strategist, to forge sharp and effective swords, demonstrating his pivotal role in the state's weapon production.

In addition to his craftsmanship, Xue Zhu also held an official position in Yue, where he oversaw swordsmanship training, indicating his broader involvement in military affairs beyond sword-making. Despite his contributions, he faced personal adversity, having been harmed by Feng Huzi (风胡子), another figure associated with sword-making. Xue Zhu also collaborated with his senior, Feng, in the process of forging swords, highlighting his teamwork and dedication to his craft.

Overall, Xue Zhu is remembered as a key figure in Yue's history, combining technical skill, official duties, and resilience in the face of challenges to contribute to the state's military and artisanal legacy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2a72fd2ce03a23a58c65d98d2258f3e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f20b87683fe0cc8608a321ff18feb71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b2a680eed881fd86d938031d895d21e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e93cef7b7f368309937f9f274b9ad084&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f89960ee186e8b69358a7a5c384a3ee9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68f026ecd42e4615bd879cf8153930c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-202f8c1ca090fa6fcaacd1c6e19d8001</data>
