    <node id="文种">
      <data key="d0">文种</data>
      <data key="d1">人物</data>
      <data key="d2">Wen Zhong (文种) was a prominent official and strategist of the Yue Kingdom during the Spring and Autumn Period in ancient China. He served as a senior minister (大夫) under King Goujian (勾践) and played a pivotal role in the kingdom's recovery and eventual triumph over the rival Wu Kingdom. Wen Zhong was renowned for his wisdom and strategic acumen, often acting as a trusted advisor and counselor to Goujian. He collaborated closely with Fan Li (范蠡), another key figure in Yue's resurgence, and together they worked to restore the kingdom's strength following its defeat and subjugation by Wu.

One of Wen Zhong's notable contributions was his proposal of the "Nine Strategies for Destroying Wu" (灭吴九术), a comprehensive plan aimed at undermining and ultimately defeating the Wu Kingdom. His efforts, alongside Fan Li's, were instrumental in Yue's successful campaign to overthrow Wu and reclaim its sovereignty. Wen Zhong's loyalty and dedication to Goujian were evident throughout his service, as he consistently provided counsel and support during the kingdom's most challenging times.

In addition to his political and military achievements, Wen Zhong shared a close friendship with Fan Li. Historical accounts mention that he was entrusted with the task of visiting Fan Li, highlighting the mutual respect and camaraderie between the two statesmen. Wen Zhong's legacy is remembered as one of strategic brilliance and unwavering commitment to the restoration and prosperity of the Yue Kingdom.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2a72fd2ce03a23a58c65d98d2258f3e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb8a415d6907f0cafb86835c412854f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6f4631a6bc7286dd9560f06b9845d9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f20b87683fe0cc8608a321ff18feb71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f3e590b3ab7f94ee3770d3739196401&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b2a680eed881fd86d938031d895d21e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-170ae9c218e79ffcd211a28e4c5e28c1</data>
