    <node id="西施">
      <data key="d0">西施</data>
      <data key="d1">人物</data>
      <data key="d2">Xishi (西施), also known as "Xizi" (西子), is a renowned beauty from the ancient Yue Kingdom during the Spring and Autumn Period of Chinese history. She is celebrated for her extraordinary beauty and is often associated with the phrase "Xizi holding her heart" (西子捧心), which highlights her delicate and graceful demeanor. Xishi played a significant role in the political and historical narrative of her time, as she was sent by the Yue Kingdom to the Wu Kingdom as part of a strategic plan to weaken the Wu ruler, King Fuchai (夫差). Her presence in the Wu royal palace, specifically in the luxurious Guanwa Palace (馆娃宫), was intended to distract and beguile King Fuchai, ultimately contributing to the downfall of the Wu Kingdom.

Xishi is also closely linked to Fan Li (范蠡), a prominent Yue strategist and statesman. She is described as the woman Fan Li deeply loved and cherished, with their relationship often portrayed as one of profound emotional connection. Fan Li is said to have harbored deep feelings for Xishi, and she is frequently depicted as his romantic partner and source of emotional solace. Despite her pivotal role in the political intrigue between the Yue and Wu Kingdoms, Xishi's story is also remembered for its romantic and tragic undertones, reflecting her dual significance as both a historical figure and a symbol of beauty and love in Chinese culture.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2a72fd2ce03a23a58c65d98d2258f3e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-013870c1938481d1558d4c2e439c83d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb8a415d6907f0cafb86835c412854f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f3e590b3ab7f94ee3770d3739196401&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-939cc8f0980bb7b81255939246f7fe66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f89960ee186e8b69358a7a5c384a3ee9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-170ae9c218e79ffcd211a28e4c5e28c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-202f8c1ca090fa6fcaacd1c6e19d8001&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0218fd37bc9158eb3bd779e577f09de5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ffa6c388cbf112774dc307d94b2500d</data>
