    <node id="夫差">
      <data key="d0">夫差</data>
      <data key="d1">人物</data>
      <data key="d2">夫差 was a ruler of the ancient state of Wu during the Spring and Autumn Period in Chinese history. He is most notably remembered as the adversary of Goujian, the king of the neighboring state of Yue. Their rivalry is a central theme in historical and legendary accounts, with Goujian ultimately defeating Wu after a prolonged struggle. Historical records suggest that夫差 fell victim to Goujian's strategic schemes, which contributed to his eventual downfall.

夫差's reign is often characterized by his indulgence in luxury and his infatuation with beauty, which weakened the state of Wu both politically and militarily. His relationship with Xishi, a renowned beauty of the era, is frequently mentioned in historical and literary sources. Xishi, who was sent to Wu as part of Goujian's plan to undermine夫差, played a significant role in the narrative of his decline.夫差's focus on personal pleasures and extravagance is cited as a major factor in the erosion of Wu's strength and stability.

Despite his initial military successes,夫差 ultimately suffered a decisive defeat at the hands of Goujian. Following this loss, he chose to end his life, marking the tragic conclusion of his rule.夫差's story serves as a cautionary tale in Chinese history, illustrating the dangers of neglecting governance and succumbing to personal desires at the expense of state affairs. Although夫差 does not always appear directly in historical texts, his legacy is frequently referenced in discussions of the rivalry between Wu and Yue and the broader dynamics of the Spring and Autumn Period.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2a72fd2ce03a23a58c65d98d2258f3e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6f4631a6bc7286dd9560f06b9845d9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76f36e0abe52b904e30fbb2a78b9a4a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f3e590b3ab7f94ee3770d3739196401&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b2a680eed881fd86d938031d895d21e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f89960ee186e8b69358a7a5c384a3ee9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-202f8c1ca090fa6fcaacd1c6e19d8001</data>
