    <node id="姑苏">
      <data key="d0">姑苏</data>
      <data key="d1">地点</data>
      <data key="d2">The entity 姑苏 (Gusu) is historically recognized as the capital city of the ancient state of Wu during the Spring and Autumn Period in Chinese history. It served as a significant political, cultural, and military center for the Wu state. Prominent figures such as Wen Zhong and Fan Li, both renowned strategists and advisors, are noted to have resided in Gusu, contributing to its historical importance.

Gusu was also a notable starting point for Wu state swordsmen, emphasizing its role in the cultivation and deployment of military talent. Despite its prominence, the city faced military challenges, including being invaded by forces from the neighboring state of Yue, marking a pivotal moment in the decline of Wu's power.

The descriptions collectively highlight Gusu's dual significance as both a hub of governance and strategy and a focal point of military activity and conflict during its time as Wu's capital.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2a72fd2ce03a23a58c65d98d2258f3e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76f36e0abe52b904e30fbb2a78b9a4a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f3e590b3ab7f94ee3770d3739196401&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f89960ee186e8b69358a7a5c384a3ee9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-202f8c1ca090fa6fcaacd1c6e19d8001</data>
