    <node id="吴国">
      <data key="d0">吴国</data>
      <data key="d1">地点</data>
      <data key="d2">Wu State (吴国) was an ancient Chinese kingdom that existed during the Spring and Autumn Period (770–476 BCE). It was ruled by notable kings, including Wu Wang Helü (吴王阖庐) and Wu Wang Fuchai (吴王夫差), with Fuchai being one of its most prominent and historically significant rulers. The state was characterized by its intense rivalry and enmity with Yue State (越国), which was considered its sworn enemy. This hostility defined much of Wu’s political and military activities, leading to numerous conflicts and wars between the two states. The rivalry culminated in Wu’s eventual defeat and annexation by Yue, marking the end of its prominence in Chinese history.

Wu State was the homeland of several renowned historical figures, most notably Wu Zixu (伍子胥), a loyal minister and strategist who played a pivotal role in the kingdom’s governance and military campaigns. The state was also famous for its skilled swordsmen and warriors, contributing to its reputation as a militarily capable and formidable kingdom. Wu served as the setting for various historical and legendary events, reflecting its importance in the cultural and political landscape of the era. Additionally, the state is associated with figures such as Xi Shi (西施), a legendary beauty whose story is intertwined with the rivalry between Wu and Yue.

Despite its power and influence during its peak, Wu State ultimately fell to Yue State, ending its reign as a significant political entity. Its legacy, however, continues to be remembered through historical records and stories that highlight its rulers, conflicts, and contributions to ancient Chinese civilization.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2a72fd2ce03a23a58c65d98d2258f3e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb8a415d6907f0cafb86835c412854f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6f4631a6bc7286dd9560f06b9845d9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f20b87683fe0cc8608a321ff18feb71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42c3e318eb3b9f5e9c1bd450e13ff5b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b2a680eed881fd86d938031d895d21e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-939cc8f0980bb7b81255939246f7fe66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e93cef7b7f368309937f9f274b9ad084&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f89960ee186e8b69358a7a5c384a3ee9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f3e590b3ab7f94ee3770d3739196401&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-170ae9c218e79ffcd211a28e4c5e28c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-202f8c1ca090fa6fcaacd1c6e19d8001&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0218fd37bc9158eb3bd779e577f09de5</data>
