    <node id="青衣剑士">
      <data key="d0">青衣剑士</data>
      <data key="d1">人物</data>
      <data key="d2">The entity "青衣剑士" refers to a group of skilled swordsmen characterized by their distinctive blue attire and exceptional mastery of swordsmanship. These swordsmen are described as emissaries sent by Wu King Fuchai, tasked with delivering swords to the neighboring state of Yue. Their expertise in swordsmanship is frequently emphasized, with mentions of their ability to wield sharp, long swords with precision and finesse. 

The 青衣剑士 are noted for their remarkable combat skills, including their refined and intricate sword techniques. One account highlights a notable duel between a 青衣剑士 and a 锦衫剑士, showcasing their prowess in martial arts. The group is specifically identified as consisting of eight swordsmen, further underscoring their collective role as representatives of Wu in diplomatic or ceremonial missions involving the presentation of swords.

In summary, 青衣剑士 embodies the image of elite swordsmen from Wu, distinguished by their blue garments, exceptional swordsmanship, and their role as emissaries under the command of Wu King Fuchai.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c6f4631a6bc7286dd9560f06b9845d9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c903f2e907674391708383e3d1afe7fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42c3e318eb3b9f5e9c1bd450e13ff5b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e58ecd9d19ebc5fffab3dc66a3dbd19</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1777556761</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="锦衫剑士">
      <data key="d0">锦衫剑士</data>
      <data key="d1">人物</data>
      <data key="d2">锦衫剑士 is a swordsman associated with the royal court of Yue, an ancient kingdom in Chinese history. He is described as a palace guard serving in the Yue King's palace, where he participates in swordsmanship contests. Known for his distinctive attire, the 锦衫剑士 wears elegant brocade garments, symbolizing his elevated status or role within the court.

The 锦衫剑士 is skilled in wielding a heavy greatsword, showcasing his strength and mastery in combat. He is noted for engaging in duels with other swordsmen, including 青衣剑士 (the swordsman in blue robes), in tests of skill and technique. Additionally, he is mentioned in the context of sparring with Fan Li, a prominent historical figure from Yue known for his wisdom and contributions to the kingdom's prosperity.

Overall, 锦衫剑士 represents a figure of martial prowess and refinement, embodying the traditions of swordsmanship and loyalty within the royal court of Yue.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c6f4631a6bc7286dd9560f06b9845d9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c903f2e907674391708383e3d1afe7fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42c3e318eb3b9f5e9c1bd450e13ff5b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e58ecd9d19ebc5fffab3dc66a3dbd19</data>
