    <edge source="西施" target="范蠡">
      <data key="d7">10.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The relationship between Fan Li (范蠡) and Xi Shi (西施) is characterized by deep emotional ties and mutual affection. Fan Li harbored profound feelings for Xi Shi, and their bond is often described as one of love and devotion. Historical accounts and cultural narratives frequently highlight their close relationship, portraying Fan Li as deeply enamored with Xi Shi and cherishing her presence in his life.

Fan Li and Xi Shi's connection extended beyond mere affection, as they reportedly planned to retreat from public life together. Fan Li envisioned a future of seclusion with Xi Shi, with some accounts suggesting that they intended to live in the serene surroundings of Taihu Lake. This desire for a shared life away from societal pressures underscores the depth of their emotional attachment.

Despite the challenges and complexities of their circumstances, Fan Li remained deeply connected to Xi Shi, often longing for her and anticipating their reunion. Their relationship is frequently described as one marked by enduring love and emotional entanglement, reflecting the significant role Xi Shi played in Fan Li's life and his unwavering devotion to her.</data>
